==Getting thrown out==

When failing to pickpocket a H.A.M. member, players will either receive the message {{mes|You feel slightly concussed from the blow.}} or {{mes|Your agility helps you partially avoid the blow.}} Upon receiving three slight concussions, the chat box will read {{mes|You're beaten unconscious and bundled out of the HAM camp.}} and players get removed from the [[H.A.M. Hideout]] (see map below), or locked up in the prison inside the hideout.

However, a high [[Agility]] level increases the chances of partially avoiding the blow, which will not count toward the three concussions before being kicked out &ndash; at level 99 Agility, players can stay in the hideout nearly indefinitely, regardless of Thieving level. Being kicked out or voluntarily leaving and re-entering the hideout resets the concussion count back to zero.

In addition to Agility level, a player can reduce their chances of being put in jail or thrown outside by wearing [[H.A.M. robes]]. Each individual piece of the H.A.M. equipment reduces the chance to be booted from the hideout by about 4%; a full set of all seven pieces thus lowers the chance by roughly 28%.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1277299184199176192|date=28 June 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/97591|archivedate=8 September 2020}} However, neither wearing H.A.M. robes nor having a high Agility level increases the chances of successful pickpockets.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/751400357473947648|date=8 July 2016|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/97065|archivedate=20 December 2019|quote=HAM kit doesn't reduce getting caught, but each piece makes you slightly less likely to be ejected after being caught.}}

